  "articleBody": "It's a common frustration to get to the end of a project and feel like something's off with your new backsplash. Often, issues stem from not getting the foundational steps right. For instance, if your countertops weren't installed first, you might find alignment problems later on. Or, if the wall prep wasn't smooth, the tiles won't lay flat. We’ve seen it all, from misaligned patterns to issues with outlet cuts that just don't sit right.\n\nA big one is using grout where caulk should be, especially at that crucial joint between the countertop and the backsplash. Grout isn't flexible enough for that spot and will crack over time. Also, rushing the cure times for mortar or adhesive before grouting can lead to long-term problems. The materials need their full time to set properly. If you're tackling a DIY project and run into these snags, don't worry, you're not alone. Sometimes, a professional eye can spot these issues and correct them before they become bigger headaches. We're here to help homeowners in the Denver area like you get the results they really want, so if you're feeling stuck, give us a shout. We serve Aurora, Centennial, and many other surrounding communities.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
